## 3. Smoke Testing vs Sanity Testing

| Point                   | Smoke Testing                                                                  | Sanity Testing                                                                            |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Purpose**             | Checks whether the major functions of a new build work.                        | Checks whether a specific change or bug fix works correctly.                              |
| **Scope**               | Broad but shallow.                                                             | Narrow but more focused.                                                                  |
| **When performed**      | Usually after receiving a new build.                                           | Usually after a minor change or bug fix.                                                  |
| **Example – Instagram** | Check login, home feed, profile and basic post loading after a new build.      | If a bug in uploading posts is fixed, test only the post-upload issue.                    |
| **Example – Paytm**     | Check login, balance display, recharge and basic navigation after a new build. | If a recharge calculation bug is fixed, mainly verify the corrected recharge calculation. |
| **Main Goal**           | Decide whether the build is stable enough for further testing.                 | Decide whether the particular change/fix is working properly.                             |

**Easy way to remember:**
**Smoke = “Is the build basically working?”**
**Sanity = “Did this particular fix/change work?”**

---

## 4. Spotify Crash After Major Update

**Smoke testing should be performed first.**

Since the app is crashing on startup after a major update, the basic functionality of the build is already affected. Smoke testing can quickly determine whether the new build is stable enough for further detailed testing. If the app cannot even start, detailed sanity testing would not be useful yet.
